{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"746813633853653032","content":"i think us not having the secret societies, or at least devaluing their importance, will greatly aid in removing that.  but I mean even at my table of 6-9 i defiantly interact with some players more than others, and have to make a conscious effort to be as inclusive as possible.\n\nthe players will always pick their favorite DMs to deal with, which makes it harder.  Being aware of the problem in general should greatly help in removing it","created_at":"2020-08-25T23:58:24.930000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747968155846180874","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746813633853653032","content":"Its the suits dilemma. Players can sort of be oversimplified into clubs, diamonds, spades or hearts. \nClubs are here to bash things. Sometimes called \"murder hobos.\" they are here to experience the fantasy of being capable of taking on conflict with  the combat kits that they are provided with. People will complain that they don't respect the socially delicate scenes. Diamonds are here for loot, or in our case dominion level play.  These players tend to be our rule lawyers. - minmaxers are typically hybrids of clubs and diamonds. Spades are here to dig for lore and story or just to try things out to see how they work. They will ask you questions that you have no idea how to answer, and tend to be the sort that look for swiss army knife applications (using things, usually hilariously such as season 2's one million ball bearings) to accomplish tasks in a way you wont expect. I am 100% this kind of player and I know how irritating it can be (fastfriends on as many npcs as there are available). Hearts are here just for the community, and in battle the long wait times can dishearten them. They also tend to be the ones that sort of give up on crafting or participating in certain aspects of the game. Once again, there usually isn't a wrong way to play, and people shouldn't be told that they are having the wrong kind of fun unless its actually detrimental.","created_at":"2020-08-26T00:10:34.915000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-26T00:16:41.157000Z","id":"747971217625055242","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
